{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00265",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.13,
      "end_seconds": 4.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, I couldn't find the door at first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.33,
      "end_seconds": 9.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.37,
      "end_seconds": 14.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.66,
      "end_seconds": 19.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Uh, I'm here because of blood in my urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.59,
      "end_seconds": 25.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "And when did that start? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.11,
      "end_seconds": 33.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "It started yesterday. My sister suggested writing things down, you know, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.35,
      "end_seconds": 36.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.81,
      "end_seconds": 47.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "It was red twice this week goes along with it, most of the time. I've been passing small clots too, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.06,
      "end_seconds": 53.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Have you had blood in your urine before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.21,
      "end_seconds": 60.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.62,
      "end_seconds": 64.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.99,
      "end_seconds": 76.53,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.83,
      "end_seconds": 81.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any pain on passing urine or flank pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.75,
      "end_seconds": 87.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.7,
      "end_seconds": 93.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any difficulty passing urine, weight loss or recent injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.47,
      "end_seconds": 99.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "No, no difficulty passing urine, weight loss or recent injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.36,
      "end_seconds": 101.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Have you had any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.38,
      "end_seconds": 104.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 105.82,
      "end_seconds": 109.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.03,
      "end_seconds": 115.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.22,
      "end_seconds": 123.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Alright, any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.92,
      "end_seconds": 125.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.06,
      "end_seconds": 128.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.6,
      "end_seconds": 131.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.1,
      "end_seconds": 135.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.16,
      "end_seconds": 137.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.11,
      "end_seconds": 143.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 144.41,
      "end_seconds": 151.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "It's amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day for my pressure, doctor. She takes hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.63,
      "end_seconds": 156.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.59,
      "end_seconds": 157.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.69,
      "end_seconds": 166.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Alright, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.82,
      "end_seconds": 169.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.57,
      "end_seconds": 173.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.04,
      "end_seconds": 177.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.03,
      "end_seconds": 183.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.8,
      "end_seconds": 189.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.66,
      "end_seconds": 192.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "So, has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.28,
      "end_seconds": 208.46,
      "duration_seconds": 14.18,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.9,
      "end_seconds": 214.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.91,
      "end_seconds": 221.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes. Yes, eczema. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.32,
      "end_seconds": 227.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.17,
      "end_seconds": 230.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.3,
      "end_seconds": 233.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.33,
      "end_seconds": 248.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.33,
      "end_seconds": 261.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.16,
      "end_seconds": 278.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 112 over 81, respiratory rate 14, pulse is 83 beats a minute, temperature 37.0."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.34,
      "end_seconds": 280.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.11,
      "end_seconds": 299.58,
      "duration_seconds": 18.47,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.71,
      "end_seconds": 302.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.05,
      "end_seconds": 307.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.9,
      "end_seconds": 310.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.33,
      "end_seconds": 328.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Abdomen is soft, no masses, and no tenderness in the loins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.79,
      "end_seconds": 351.06,
      "duration_seconds": 19.27,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is blood in the urine that needs full investigation. I'd also keep a urine infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.06,
      "end_seconds": 357.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.78,
      "end_seconds": 375.01,
      "duration_seconds": 16.23,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like blood in the urine that needs full investigation, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had blood in your urine, yesterday, and no pain on passing urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.73,
      "end_seconds": 380.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.9,
      "end_seconds": 397.75,
      "duration_seconds": 15.85,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.34,
      "end_seconds": 401.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I mean, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.29,
      "end_seconds": 409.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "I'm going to order a cystoscopy, for haematuria. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.76,
      "end_seconds": 411.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.71,
      "end_seconds": 434.81,
      "duration_seconds": 22.1,
      "text": "Let's get a urine culture, for haematuria. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We should do a CT scan of the kidneys and bladder for haematuria. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Keep drinking plenty of water, and let us know quickly if you pass clots or can't pass urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.59,
      "end_seconds": 453.49,
      "duration_seconds": 13.9,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. I'd like you to see the urology clinic as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 454.87,
      "end_seconds": 455.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.95,
      "end_seconds": 463.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you can't pass urine or pass large clots, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.98,
      "end_seconds": 465.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.0,
      "end_seconds": 470.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 471.19,
      "end_seconds": 475.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 476.58,
      "end_seconds": 481.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 482.8,
      "end_seconds": 487.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "So, I come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 487.92,
      "end_seconds": 492.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 492.74,
      "end_seconds": 495.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}